{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_782430466#10_1648056615","relevance":2,"reason":"This consumer diabetes/dairy article cites meta-analysis evidence that dairy, particularly yogurt, may protect against type 2 diabetes, but it is not dedicated to yogurt use or a primary scientific evidence synthesis.","learned":"Consumer diabetes guidance commonly cites meta-analytic evidence that yogurt consumption may be protective against type 2 diabetes."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"yogurt consumption\" \"type 2 diabetes\" \"prospective cohort studies\")","reason":"Search for the likely dedicated epidemiologic meta-analysis title/content on yogurt consumption and type 2 diabetes risk in prospective cohort studies."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"yogurt consumption\" \"type 2 diabetes\" \"prospective cohort studies\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_276413029#4_609994493","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q108","rank":4,"snippet":"Your Health and the Planet’s Health Purchase Make Serve Did You Know? Terms of Use \" , \"segment\": \"6] Learn more about the body’s microbiome. Epidemiological research on specific health effects of yogurt is still limited but a few studies suggest a benefit. In a study following three large cohorts for up to 20 years that included 120,877 men and women free of obesity and chronic diseases at baseline, <cover>yogurt consumption appeared to protect from weight gain. [ 7] The authors suggested that changes in colonic bacteria from eating the yogurt may have influenced weight changes. Daily yogurt intake may also protect against heart disease and type 2 diabetes. [ 8,9] Two meta-analyses of prospective cohort studies </cover>found an 18% and 14% lower risk of developing type 2 diabetes with daily yogurt intake. [ 10,11] Why yogurt affects diabetes is unclear, but it is believed that helpful bacteria in the yogurt may reduce inflammation or improve the action of the body’s natural insulin. For Your Health and the Planet’s Health The production of dairy foods places considerable demand on land, water, and other natural resources, and dairy-producing ruminant animals like ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_666414104#5_1372961873","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_666414104#4_1372960295","rank":2,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_666414104#6_1372963293","rank":3,"relevance":2}]}}
